WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.660
Speaker 1: This morning we woke up to what
was reported as a shocking number 33 percent,

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:13.300
33 percent approval for President Joe Biden,
a disastrously low number and the number is

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:18.450
true. But we're going to contextualize it.
It's just one poll. And while overall Joe

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:24.470
Biden's approval is not great, it's still
better than Trump's was at this point in time

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:32.220
in Trump's presidency. So without context,
the 33 percent number is not worth that much,

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:37.150
but it is not a good number. So let's start
with that 33 percent number. We have a new

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:44.700
Quinnipiac poll and indeed the poll finds,
and Quinnipiac is a good, good pollster that

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:53.611
only 33 percent of Americans approve of the
way that Joe Biden is handling his job. This

00:00:53.611 --> 00:01:02.390
is a tie for the low ever received by Biden
in this poll. With January 12th, when it was

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:13.179
also 33 percent, now the main question for
me is why is it low and what could raise it

00:01:13.179 --> 00:01:17.389
really the key to questions with any presidential
approval poll? But then we're also going to

00:01:17.389 --> 00:01:24.229
compare it to other approval polls. So looking
at the Quinnipiac poll, we find that only

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:31.909
39 percent of Americans approve of Joe Biden's
handling of the response to the Russian invasion

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:38.959
of Ukraine 39 percent. That's a much lower
number than we saw weeks ago in other polls.

00:01:38.959 --> 00:01:44.609
Now, part of it could be the way the poll
is done, and part of it likely is a decline

00:01:44.609 --> 00:01:50.710
in approval of how Joe Biden has handled that
situation. Interestingly, more than eight

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.590
in 10 Americans believe Russian President
Vladimir Putin is a war criminal, something

00:01:54.590 --> 00:02:00.559
that Donald Trump hesitates to say, and we
will get to that a little bit later. 10 percent

00:02:00.559 --> 00:02:06.749
believe Putin is not a war criminal. Seven
in 10 think Putin ordered Russian troops to

00:02:06.749 --> 00:02:14.110
kill civilians in Ukraine. 14 percent think
that he did not. So this is the Quinnipiac

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:19.810
poll. Well, what about more, generally speaking,
what's going on with Joe Biden's approval?

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:25.519
Well, for that, one of the best places to
look is the FiveThirtyEight Biden approval,

00:02:25.519 --> 00:02:31.430
which looks at an average of recent approval
polls. And when we look there, we find that

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:37.930
it's not as bad for Joe Biden. Certainly,
it's not good. And as you can see early in

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:43.799
his presidency, Joe Biden in the mid-50s in
terms of approval, then moving into the low

00:02:43.799 --> 00:02:51.170
50s crossing below the 50 percent line, getting
down into the mid-40s and then into the low

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:56.989
40s. And most recently, we see this little
decline from about forty two to forty one.

00:02:56.989 --> 00:03:02.040
If you look more deeply at the specific polls
making that up, and this is where we would

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:08.680
say, OK, what is where does the Quinnipiac
poll fit into this? We see that the Quinnipiac

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:14.609
this recent Quinnipiac University poll is
here, which has Joe Biden at 33. That is an

00:03:14.609 --> 00:03:21.050
outlier in the sense that all of the other
recent polls have Joe Biden between 38 and

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:25.750
44. Does that mean the Quinnipiac poll is
wrong? Well, no, it doesn't mean it's wrong,

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:30.909
but it does mean it is sort of an outlier.
And when FiveThirtyEight applies what they

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:38.849
call an adjustment, the three becomes 37.
So needless to say, this is not a good situation

00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:44.909
for Joe Biden. And the question now is going
to be, well, what needs to happen for that

00:03:44.909 --> 00:03:52.180
to change because these are not great numbers.
The next question would be are these guaranteed

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:57.959
to be destructive numbers, looking forward
at the midterms and potentially at 2024? Well,

00:03:57.959 --> 00:04:05.790
one thing we can look at there. Is how does
the current Biden approval? Forty one point

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:11.650
something, how does that compare with other
presidents at this point in their presidencies?

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:17.940
If you look at Biden versus Trump, you find
that at this point in time, Trump actually

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:23.530
was at forty point six. I mean, it's more
or less the same. But Biden's approval today

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:29.569
is slightly better than was Trump's at this
point in his presidency. If you compare Biden

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:34.530
to basically any other recent president, you
see that Barack Obama had a higher approval.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:40.729
At this point in time, George W. Bush had
a dramatically higher approval thanks to 911.

00:04:40.729 --> 00:04:45.560
Bill Clinton had a higher approval than Biden.
George H.W. Bush had a much higher approval

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:49.420
than Biden. Reagan had a higher approval than
by, but you have to go all the way back to

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:56.840
Jimmy Carter to even get close. And even then,
just at this time, Carter also did better

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.930
than Biden. But soon Jimmy Carter started
seeing a reduction. What does this mean for

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:06.611
twenty twenty two? It's not good. It's not
good. There's really no way to spin it. That

00:05:06.611 --> 00:05:14.699
feels empirically honest. And I know that
you're going to see hot takes from Democratic

00:05:14.699 --> 00:05:19.320
pollsters and operatives and analysts that
are saying, Well, listen, the midterms are

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:25.780
not necessarily a referendum on Biden and
x y z. But if this doesn't change, it's going

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:31.949
to be a disaster for Democrats. There's just
no way around it. It is going to be potentially

00:05:31.949 --> 00:05:35.940
one of the worst midterms for Democrats in
a very long time now. What could change it?

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:41.270
Many things could change it if the American
perception of the economy improves between

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:46.460
now and November. It's good for Democrats,
and I know many of you will say, but David,

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:49.900
the numbers are good for the economy. You're
absolutely right. But we did a story early

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:55.120
last week about the difference between an
economic reality and a political reality.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.669
Jobs numbers are dramatically better now than
when Joe Biden took over, but a third of the

00:05:58.669 --> 00:06:02.940
country doesn't think so. A third of the country
thinks jobs have been lost. I know we can

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:07.830
say, Oh, those stupid, if that's what they
believe, they're going to vote on that basis.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:13.970
And so what matters is what people, what people
believe some kind of satisfactory resolution

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:17.800
in Ukraine, and it's hard to use that language.
Given the death and destruction that's been

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:23.300
seen there. Some kind of politically satisfactory
resolution will likely be helpful to Democrats

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:27.050
because I believe that the midterms are a
referendum on Joe Biden. I think there's no

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:32.390
way to argue that that they are not but not
good numbers for Joe Biden. And if nothing

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:37.190
changes, that's the key if nothing changes.
It will be a disastrous midterm for Democrats.

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:42.400
If you disagree with me. Let me know. Tell
me how the current numbers translate to an

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.960
OK midterm for Democrats. I just don't see
it

